                  <provenance type="#s"><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_295">Lanthony (secunda),
                        Gloucestershire. Augustinian priory of St Mary the Virgin and St John the
                        Baptist</orgName><p>The acceptance of the Lanthony provenance is tentative
                        and based on the script, which looks like Lanthony style.</p><p>"D. M." in
                        margins (pt. ii).</p><p>The entry in the catalogue that would correspond to
                        this volume ('Bernardus de gracia et libero arbitrio. Chirt') makes
                        reference to the vicar of Cherington, a priory manor in east
                        Gloucestershire, who held a clutch of priory books. Reference to this would
                        be expected in the book itself but is not found; however, it would have been
                        on a flyleaf that was lost when these leaves were combined with two other
                        units to form the present volume.</p></provenance>
